; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; What burning looks like.
;
; The client owns the KINDS of effect and this file owns every number in them, so
; a new burning thing is a block here rather than a class. The kinds:
;
;   FLAME_TRAIL   sparks left behind along the line of flight
;   GLOW_ORB      a glowing body, for a projectile that has no model
;   IMPACT_BURST  a burst of sparks and a flash of light where it lands
;   GLOW_PARTS    named pieces of a model lit from inside -- eye sockets, runes,
;                 the coals in a brazier. The one that is not about something in
;                 flight, and the cheapest by a distance: one material and no
;                 light. Which is what makes it affordable on EVERY creature in a
;                 room, where a torch each would be over the light budget before
;                 the second one.
;
; A thing may have all three. A name this client does not know is ignored with a
; warning rather than refused -- an arrow whose trail is missing still arrives.
;
; The LIGHT is the part worth the trouble. This is a dark game and a burning
; thing crossing a room is the only moving light in it; the terrain shader was
; taught to read four of them for exactly this. Everything else here is dressing
; on top of that.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Effect layers
;
; An effect is several things at once, and has to be. A single kind of particle
; looks like a single kind of particle -- a burst of orange dots is a diagram of
; an explosion. What reads as one is a flash that is gone before it is seen, fire
; that blooms and dies, smoke that rises slower and outlives it, sparks thrown
; further than either, and a ring saying how far it reached. So an effect is a
; handful of these blocks, named by the effect and then by the layer, and drawn
; in the order they are written, each over the last.
;
; A new effect is blocks here. A new TYPE of layer is code, and there are ten:
;
;   BURST   everything at once from one point, then gone
;   TRAIL   let out behind something moving and left hanging where it was let out
;   RING    lying on the floor and opening outward
;   AURA    around a creature and going where it goes, for as long as the skill
;   IMPACT  a flash: one or a few large shapes that bloom and are gone
;   ARC     a cut, laid on the floor facing the way the blow went
;   BEAM    a line from where a run began to where it ended
;   PILLAR  a column of light on the floor, coming DOWN onto someone or rising UP
;   MARK    lying on the floor and staying -- a warning, a scorch
;   LIGHT   a light: flaring and fading, or carried by what burns
;
; When it plays follows from the type. On a SKILL's look everything plays at the
; cast. On a PROJECTILE's effect, TRAIL, AURA and a LIGHT with no Seconds are
; carried while it flies, and everything else plays where it lands.
;
; Blend is the one choice that is easy to get backwards. Additive is LIGHT --
; fire, magic, sparks, flashes -- and two of them overlapping are brighter than
; one, as light is. Alpha is STUFF -- smoke, dust, a scorch -- and covers what is
; behind it. Smoke drawn additively lights up the floor it is meant to be hiding.
;
; Cover sits between the two, 0 to 1: how much of what is behind a layer it hides
; while it adds its own colour. Light alone vanishes into a pale floor -- orange
; added to pale stone is a pale smudge -- so fire hides a little of the ground it
; burns over and keeps its colour on grass and stone alike. Leave it out and it is
; 0 for Additive and 1 for Alpha.
;
; Every texture is a white shape. Colour is the layer's: born at the first of
; Colour and dying at the second, along ColourEase. Size, the same, along
; SizeEase. A curve is the whole of the feel: 1 is a straight line, which is
; what a machine does; 2 to 4 changes fast and settles, as a thing that was
; struck does; -2 to -4 holds and then changes late, as a thing arriving does.
;
;   Count        how many; for anything let out over time, how many at once
;   Rate         how many a second over time, or nothing for all at once
;   Delay        seconds after the moment -- what lets smoke rise out of a fire
;   Seconds      how long a lasting layer lasts. Leave it out and it lasts as
;                long as the SKILL does -- its duration, its wind-up, or the slow
;                it lays on whoever it caught -- so the number is written once
;   Life         the shortest and longest a particle lives
;   Size         born, and dying; SizeJitter how much each may differ
;   Alpha        how solid it is born, and dying
;   FadeIn       fraction of its life spent appearing; FadeOut, disappearing
;   Speed        slowest and fastest it leaves at
;   Direction    UP DOWN OUT ALL FORWARD BACK NONE; Spread, how far off it
;   Radius       how far from the middle it may be born; Height, above the floor.
;                A PILLAR stands from the floor to its Height, and goes UP or DOWN
;   Gravity      pull downward; negative rises. Drag, how the air slows it
;   Stretch      how much a fast particle is drawn out along its speed
;   Spin         degrees a second. Turn, the angle it is born at; TurnJitter,
;                how much it may be turned at random -- 360 for smoke, 0 for
;                anything that has to point somewhere
;   PulseRate    breaths a second, PulseDepth how deep. On an AURA only in the
;                last FadeOut of its run: how a shield says it is about to go
;   At           SPOT FROM TO BOTH PATH CASTER CAUGHT -- where it happens
;   Fall         how far above its spot a carried layer starts, brought down
;                over Seconds. What a meteor is
;   Rise         a PILLAR's: how much of its life the end that moves takes to cross
;                the whole Height. RiseEase, the curve it crosses along
;   Follows      Yes keeps a layer on whoever it happened to, going where he goes,
;                for as long as it lasts. An AURA always does
;   Order        there is no such field: layers that start together are drawn in
;                the order they are written, each over the last -- so what lies
;                on the floor goes first, smoke next, and fire and light last.
;                A scorch written after the fire is a dark disc laid over it
;   Measure      Units, or Reach: Size and Radius counted in the skill's own
;                Radius, so a Size of 2 is exactly as wide as the skill reaches.
;                For the shapes that MEAN how far it went -- a warning, a rim --
;                so they cannot be tuned apart from the skill
;
; ★ An effect with layers is drawn by its layers alone. Of its Effect
; block only ShakeSeconds and ShakePower are still read: there is one camera, so
; every knock goes through the one place that decides which knock wins.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Effect
  Name = FlameArrow
  Kinds = [FLAME_TRAIL, IMPACT_BURST]
  Colour = 0xFFD98A
  FadeColour = 0xB02400
  LightColour = 0xFF8A28
  ; Power is how hard it burns and Radius how far it reaches. This is the one
  ; shot the player chose to spend, so it is the one worth lighting the room for.
  LightPower = 3.4
  LightRadius = 78
  ; Sixty sparks alive at once, each for two thirds of a second. This is the
  ; player's ultimate arrow rather than something forty of fly a fight, so it can
  ; afford to be a real fire -- the ceilings further down are what keep an
  ; ordinary shot cheap.
  Particles = 60
  ParticleSize = 3.4
  ParticleLife = 0.62
  Spread = 9
  BurstParticles = 48
  BurstSize = 4.5
  BurstSeconds = 0.45

  Layers = [
    ; Her heavy arrow. In flight: a bright head, fire let out behind it, sparks shed
    ; off it and the light it carries. Where it lands: a flash, a small burst of fire,
    ; sparks thrown hard and a puff of smoke -- an arrow, not a fireball, so it is the
    ; sparks that are big and the fire that is small.
    Layer
      Name = Head
      Type = AURA
      Texture = effects/particles/circle_05.png
      Blend = Additive
      Cover = 0.3
      Count = 6
      Rate = 40
      Life = [0.1, 0.16]
      Size = [8, 5]
      Colour = [0xFFF0C0, 0xFFA040]
      Alpha = [1, 0.5]
    End

    Layer
      Name = Fire
      Type = TRAIL
      Texture = effects/particles/fire_01.png
      Blend = Additive
      Cover = 0.4
      Count = 40
      Rate = 90
      Life = [0.18, 0.3]
      Size = [7, 2]
      SizeEase = 2
      SizeJitter = 0.3
      Colour = [0xFFC060, 0xA02000]
      ColourEase = 2
      Alpha = [1, 0]
      Speed = [1, 3]
      Direction = ALL
      Drag = 2
      Gravity = -6
      Spin = 120
    End

    Layer
      Name = Embers
      Type = TRAIL
      Texture = effects/particles/star_04.png
      Blend = Additive
      Count = 16
      Rate = 28
      Life = [0.3, 0.5]
      Size = [1.4, 0.2]
      Colour = [0xFFE6A8, 0xFF6A10]
      Speed = [4, 10]
      Direction = ALL
      Drag = 1.5
      Gravity = 20
    End

    Layer
      Name = Glow
      Type = LIGHT
      LightColour = 0xFF8A28
      LightPower = 3.4
      LightRadius = 78
    End

    Layer
      Name = Flash
      Type = IMPACT
      Texture = effects/particles/star_08.png
      Blend = Additive
      Count = 1
      Life = [0.14, 0.14]
      Size = [6, 26]
      SizeEase = 3
      Colour = [0xFFFFFF, 0xFFC060]
      Alpha = [1, 0]
      FadeOut = 0.6
      Height = 5
      TurnJitter = 45
    End

    Layer
      Name = Burst
      Type = BURST
      Texture = effects/particles/fire_02.png
      Blend = Additive
      Cover = 0.5
      Count = 8
      Life = [0.3, 0.45]
      Size = [6, 14]
      SizeEase = 2.5
      SizeJitter = 0.3
      Colour = [0xFFC060, 0x8A1800]
      Alpha = [1, 0]
      FadeOut = 0.5
      Speed = [8, 16]
      Direction = UP
      Spread = 80
      Drag = 4
      Gravity = -6
      Spin = 60
      Height = 3
    End

    Layer
      Name = Sparks
      Type = BURST
      Texture = effects/particles/star_04.png
      Blend = Additive
      Count = 22
      Life = [0.3, 0.55]
      Size = [1.6, 0.25]
      Stretch = 0.06
      Colour = [0xFFF0B8, 0xFF7020]
      Speed = [30, 70]
      Direction = OUT
      Spread = 55
      Drag = 2.5
      Gravity = 40
      Height = 3
    End

    Layer
      Name = Puff
      Type = BURST
      Texture = effects/particles/smoke_03.png
      Blend = Alpha
      Delay = 0.05
      Count = 4
      Life = [0.6, 0.9]
      Size = [6, 12]
      SizeEase = 2
      Colour = [0x6A605A, 0x3A3634]
      Alpha = [0.45, 0]
      Speed = [3, 6]
      Direction = UP
      Spread = 60
      Drag = 2
      Gravity = -5
      Spin = 30
      Height = 3
    End

    Layer
      Name = Light
      Type = LIGHT
      Seconds = 0.3
      LightColour = 0xFF9A40
      LightPower = 3
      LightRadius = 64
      FadeOut = 0.85
    End
  ]
End
